name 'building-data-driven-systems-postassessment-q10_2025'

question 'You notice that on a mobile device, a rendered list of data is overflowing the screen horizontally. Which step in the "Data-to-Display" process likely needs revision?'

wrong 'The schema needs more fields.'
wrong 'The `.map()` method is not running fast enough.'
right 'The visual rendering (CSS/HTML) needs to be adjusted for responsive design and clarity.'
wrong 'The original array should be converted into a single string.'

allow_multiple_attempts false

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 6

Evaluation of a rendered list involves checking for accessibility and readability. Horizontal overflow is a common UI/UX issue that requires adjusting the display logic or styles. 
MARKDOWN
